1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,500
The defendant was seen near the harbor on the evening of the murder.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
We will demonstrate beyond a reasonable doubt exactly who is responsible.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Detective, please describe what you found at the crime scene.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The victim was a wealthy shipping magnate with many powerful enemies.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
His business partner stood to inherit the entire company.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The ledger reveals a pattern of embezzlement spanning many years.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
On the night in question a storm rolled in off the ocean.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The lighthouse keeper heard a single gunshot just after midnight.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
No one could have crossed the flooded causeway in that weather.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Which means the killer was already inside the mansion.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The safe had been opened and the emerald necklace was missing.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Our forensic team recovered a torn piece of a sailor's jacket.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The threads match a coat found in the gardener's cottage.

14
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
But the gardener has an ironclad alibi for the whole evening.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
So we must ask who else had access to that private dock.

16
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The answer lies buried in the shipping manifests from last spring.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Follow the money and you will always find the motive.

18
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Tomorrow we will call our final witness to the stand.
